      {
         "id": "c",
         "prompt": "Let \\( S \\) be the region bounded by the graphs of \\( f \\) and \\( g \\) and the vertical line \\( x = 5 \\). Find the area of \\( S \\).",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "\\frac{14}{3}",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "For 4 < x < 5 the graph of g lies above the graph of f, for example g(5) = 15 > f(5) = 5.",
               "latex": "\\int_{4}^{5} \\left[(x^{2} - 2x) - (6x - x^{2})\\right] dx = \\int_{4}^{5} (2x^{2} - 8x)\\,dx"
            },
            {
               "text": "Antidifferentiate and evaluate.",
               "latex": "\\left[\\frac{2x^{3}}{3} - 4x^{2}\\right]_{4}^{5} = \\left(\\frac{250}{3} - 100\\right) - \\left(\\frac{128}{3} - 64\\right) = \\frac{14}{3}"
            }
         ],
